<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 22 December, from 1135 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1135</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen of Blois is crowned king of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after Henry I's death, his nephew Stephen was crowned at Westminster despite having sworn to support Henry's daughter, the Empress Matilda. The civil war that followed became known as the Anarchy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1715</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Old Pretender lands in Scotland, too late</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James Francis Edward Stuart landed at Peterhead to lead the Jacobite rising. After the defeat at Preston and the stalemate at Sheriffmuir in November, the cause was failing, and he sailed back to France in February.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1894</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A court martial convicts Captain Alfred Dreyfus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A French military court convicted the Jewish officer Alfred Dreyfus of passing secrets to Germany and sentenced him to deportation for life. His innocence, and the cover-up, split France in the Dreyfus Affair.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1964</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The SR-71 Blackbird makes its first flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lockheed's SR-71 reconnaissance aircraft first flew at Palmdale, California. Able to cruise above Mach 3 at about 25,000 metres, it remains the fastest crewed jet-powered aircraft.</p></li></ol>
